From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v-zhangxiaomeng5 <v-zhangxiaomeng5@xiaomi.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Apr 2026 15:58:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] libcxx/__fwd/ios.h: fix streamoff type mismatch by removing
 _NEWLIB_VERSION guard

The original guard "#if defined(_NEWLIB_VERSION)" set streamoff to long int (matching newlib's off_t). However, _NEWLIB_VERSION leaks into NuttX builds through the toolchain's newlib headers via the include chain: libcxx/math.h -> toolchain math.h -> sys/reent.h -> sys/cdefs.h -> sys/features.h -> _newlib_version.h. This leak only affects source files that transitively include math.h, causing different libcxx .cpp files to see different streamoff types - iostream.cpp gets long int while ios.instantiations.cpp gets long long, resulting in a linker error due to mismatched mangled symbols for basic_streambuf::seekoff.
NuttX uses its own libc (not newlib) with off_t = int64_t, so streamoff should always be long long. The upstream llvm is also moving away from _NEWLIB_VERSION detection toward an explicit _LIBCPP_LIBC_NEWLIB CMake-configured macro (targeting llvm-22+).

Signed-off-by: v-zhangxiaomeng5 <v-zhangxiaomeng5@xiaomi.com>
---
 include/__fwd/ios.h | 5 -----
 1 file changed, 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/__fwd/ios.h b/include/__fwd/ios.h
index 831624f4b1..abcff9abd6 100644
--- a/include/__fwd/ios.h
+++ b/include/__fwd/ios.h
@@ -31,12 +31,7 @@ using wios = basic_ios<wchar_t>;
 template <class _CharT, class _Traits>
 class _LIBCPP_PREFERRED_NAME(ios) _LIBCPP_IF_WIDE_CHARACTERS(_LIBCPP_PREFERRED_NAME(wios)) basic_ios;
 
-#if defined(_NEWLIB_VERSION)
-// On newlib, off_t is 'long int'
-using streamoff = long int; // for char_traits in <string>
-#else
 using streamoff = long long; // for char_traits in <string>
-#endif
 
 _LIBCPP_END_NAMESPACE_STD
 
